WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.130
Kiln runs open generative models inside
your Java application: language models,

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.839
images, songs, video, and audio tools.

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:13.574
You call them like any other Java
method, and they run on your GPU.

00:00:14.283 --> 00:00:18.951
If you want a local language model
or embeddings in Java, there are options.

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:22.575
They work, though they're often
slower than they should be.

00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:26.445
But what if you want to flag
a fracture on an X-ray for review?

00:00:26.445 --> 00:00:28.533
Spot defects on a production line?

00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:30.069
Read a stack of invoices?

00:00:30.069 --> 00:00:32.034
Isolate the vocals from a track?

00:00:32.034 --> 00:00:34.675
Or any of a plethora
of other capabilities?

00:00:34.675 --> 00:00:37.132
Until now, from the JVM, you were stuck.

00:00:37.132 --> 00:00:41.900
It meant a Python stack, or a tool like
ComfyUI behind HTTP: another runtime,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.933
another process,
and a network hop on every call.

00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:47.329
Kiln calls the native engines directly.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:49.847
No Python, no server, nothing in between.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.624
It uses Java's Foreign
Function and Memory API,

00:00:53.624 --> 00:00:56.960
so the call into the engine
is a plain native call.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.549
Weights load once and stay
on the GPU between requests,

00:01:00.549 --> 00:01:05.703
and when memory runs short, Kiln unloads
the models you've used least recently.

00:01:05.703 --> 00:01:09.912
Text streams back token by token,
and models can call your tools.

00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:15.193
In Kiln Studio, chat with a model
and watch the tokens per second,

00:01:15.193 --> 00:01:18.453
paint an image, write a song,
or render a clip.

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:23.941
On our test laptop, Kiln made a one-minute
song up to twice as fast as ComfyUI,

00:01:23.941 --> 00:01:25.052
on the same GPU.

00:01:25.749 --> 00:01:30.442
Pull a model from Hugging Face with
one command, and try it in Kiln Studio.

00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:34.476
Kiln is plain Java with no dependencies,
so it works in any app,

00:01:34.476 --> 00:01:38.951
and it's a great companion for Embabel
Agent: local models, in process.

00:01:39.649 --> 00:01:42.919
Here's what open models
can make, running in Kiln.

00:01:42.919 --> 00:01:45.339
This is Endless Country, episode two.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:54.638
Kiln!

00:01:54.638 --> 00:01:57.589
Open models, inside your JVM!

00:01:57.589 --> 00:02:03.084
Sponsored by Rod Johnson,
and created by Jasper Blues.

00:02:03.084 --> 00:02:03.796
kiln4j.

00:02:03.796 --> 00:02:04.203
org!
